# Docker build context exclusions.
#
# The Dockerfile does `COPY . .`. On the Space the build context is the Space
# repo, which never contains .env (gitignored, and deploy_hf.sh uses `git add
# -A`, which honours that). This file guards LOCAL `docker build` runs, where
# the context is your real working tree — without it your live Databento /
# Anthropic / OpenAI / HF keys get baked into an image layer and survive even
# if a later layer deletes them.

# Secrets
.env
.env.*
*.key
*.pem
.netrc

# Third-party research — must never enter an image.
data/reference/
Sys_Commodity.pdf
reference_paper.pdf

# VCS / build metadata. Nothing at runtime reads git.
.git
.gitattributes
.gitignore

# Python
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
dist/
build/
.pytest_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# Heavy local caches the viewer never reads. All gitignored, so absent from the
# Space context but present locally; excluding them keeps a local build from
# shipping them into the daemon.
data/raw/
data/processed/_cache/
logs/
notebooks/
specs/
.specify/
.claude/
